    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch13-24: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.62";
    dc:description "The universal quantitative prediction is highly falsifiable. Public developmental data can test examples but lack representative coverage of animal and plant rudiments.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Measure each rudiment relative to homologous adjoining structures across embryonic and adult stages and record transient rudiments that disappear. Any robust case with a smaller relative embryonic rudiment refutes the universal rule.";
